# .semgrepignore — path exclusions for semgrep (gitignore syntax).
#
# Read by the GitLab-side Probe SAST scanner (and local semgrep runs). Probe
# honors repo-root tool config files (.gitleaks.toml, .banditrc) but NOT inline
# `# nosemgrep` comments — so adjudicated false positives in NON-PRODUCTION
# files are excluded here by path.
#
# SCOPE POLICY (deliberately conservative — see issue #2314 / triage #2312):
# Only non-production files are path-excluded. Production source files are NOT
# listed here, even when they carry adjudicated-FP findings, because a path
# exclude blinds semgrep to ALL future (potentially real) findings in that file.
# Production-source FPs are handled by rule-level suppression instead, not here.
#
# Each entry below is a verified false positive (Probe scan 2026-06-28, #2312).

# --- Test directories: synthetic credentials / fixtures (#2312, r/all scan 2026-06-29) ---
# The full registry ruleset (r/all) flags hardcoded test secrets, sample JWTs,
# fake tokens and keys throughout the test suites (jwt-python-hardcoded-secret,
# detected-github-token, detected-private-key, detected-jwt-token, etc.) — 122
# such findings, all in test fixtures, none in shipping code. Tests deliberately
# embed fake secrets and are not deployed, so path-excluding test dirs is the
# safe, standard treatment. Production source is NOT excluded here (it is handled
# by rule-scoped same-line `# nosemgrep`, preserving future coverage).
tests/
modules/*/tests/
modules/*/*/tests/
modules/*/*/*/tests/
modules/*/*/*/*/tests/
**/*.test.ts

# --- Documentation & scan artifacts: sample tokens, not live secrets ---
# The semgrep baseline SARIF contains finding fingerprints (incl. token strings)
# from prior scans — scanning it is circular.
.github/security/semgrep-baseline.sarif
# Security audit note documenting allowlisted sample credentials.
data/security/2026-06-05-class-A-gitleaks-allowlist-audit.md
